.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt SLENDMAIL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm slendmail ,
.Nm sendmail ,
.Nm newaliases ,
.Nm mailq
.Nd deliver the mail of system tools to chat and webhook services
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl tiIv
.Op Fl f Ar sender
.Op Fl F Ar name
.Op Fl o Ar option
.Op Fl b Ar mode
.Op Fl q Ns Op Ar interval
.Op Fl -config Ar path
.Op Fl -
.Op Ar recipient ...
.Nm
.Fl -version | -help
.Nm newaliases
.Nm mailq
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads one message on standard input and delivers it to the targets of
.Pa /etc/slendmail.conf .
It is installed as
.Pa /usr/sbin/sendmail
and accepts the command lines of cron, at, sudo, mdadm, mailx and similar
callers.
.Pp
Flags follow
.Xr getopt 3 :
a value is glued
.Pq Fl froot
or the next argument
.Pq Fl f Ar root ,
flags without a value group
.Pq Fl ti ,
and
.Fl -
ends the options.
Options and recipients may come in any order before
.Fl - .
The value of a flag is never read as an option.
An unknown flag is logged and ignored.
.Pp
Recipients are the arguments, split at commas, and with
.Fl t
the addresses of the To, Cc and Bcc headers, without duplicates.
A message with a Resent-To, Resent-Cc or Resent-Bcc header, even an empty one,
is a resent message: then
.Fl t
takes the addresses of these three headers instead.
Bcc and Resent-Bcc headers are removed from the message.
.Pa /etc/aliases
and
.Pa .forward
are not read.
.Pp
The envelope sender is the value of
.Fl f
or
.Fl r ,
else the first Resent-From address, else the From address, else
.Ev EMAIL ,
else
.Ev USER
or
.Ev LOGNAME
at the host name, else the login name of the real user id at the host name.
When the setgid bit applies, the environment is skipped; a user id without an
entry in the user database gives an empty sender.
.Pp
The text of a notification is the text/plain part of the message, else its
text/html part converted to text; other parts are attachments.
The conversion collapses white space outside pre elements and reduces several
empty lines in a row to one everywhere, pre elements included.
Encoded words, quoted-printable and base64 are decoded and every charset is
converted to UTF-8.
A body declared US-ASCII, or in an unknown charset, that is valid UTF-8 is
taken as UTF-8.
Text without a charset or declared US-ASCII that is not valid UTF-8, and text
declared ISO-8859-1, is read as windows-1252.
.Pp
The message goes to all targets at the same time, each in the markup of its
service.
A text longer than a target accepts is cut, counted the way the service counts
it: a subject longer than a quarter of the limit is cut at a word and ends
with
.Dq ... ,
then the list of attachments and then the body, which ends with a notice.
An attachment the target sends files but not this one, over its size or number
of files, stays in the list with a notice.
.Sh TARGETS
Each
.Li "[target.NAME]"
table of the configuration is one target; its
.Ic type
selects the service:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm telegram
Bot API
.Cm sendMessage
in the HTML parse mode, text of at most 4096 characters counted in UTF-16
units after entities, and one
.Cm sendDocument
per attachment, up to 10 files of 50 MB.
.It Cm discord
One webhook execution with wait=true and no mention allowed, text of at most
2000 characters, up to 10 files of 20 MiB and 25 MiB together.
.It Cm slack
Web API
.Cm chat.postMessage
with the bot token, text of at most 40000 characters, and up to 10 files
shared in the thread of the message.
.It Cm ntfy
A JSON publish with the subject as title, text of at most 4096 bytes, and one
more message per attachment, up to 10 files of 15 MiB.
.It Cm http
One POST of the JSON document of its preset:
.Cm mattermost ,
.Cm slack-webhook
or
.Cm generic-json ;
extra headers override the Content-Type of the preset.
Only
.Cm slack-webhook
is cut, to 40000 characters.
.El
.Pp
429 and 5xx answers, and any answer with a Retry-After header, are temporary
failures; other rejections are permanent.
A target that took the text but not all files counts as delivered.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f Ar sender , Fl r Ar sender
Envelope sender, angle brackets around it removed; an empty value or
.Li <>
is the null sender.
Without a value or with a line break the call exits 64.
.It Fl F Ar name
Full name of the sender; a line break exits 64.
.It Fl t
Take recipients from the To, Cc and Bcc headers as well, or only from the
Resent-To, Resent-Cc and Resent-Bcc headers when the message has any of them.
.It Fl i , Fl oi
A line with a single dot is ordinary text.
Without it such a line ends the message, and the first dot of a line
starting with two dots is removed.
.It Fl o Ar option
Ignored, except
.Fl oi .
.It Fl b Ar mode
The first letter decides:
.Cm m
delivers, the default;
.Cm i
does nothing;
.Cm p
lists the queue;
.Cm s
is refused with exit status 64; other modes are ignored with a warning.
.It Fl q Ns Op Ar interval
Runs the queue once; the interval is ignored.
.It Fl I
Does nothing, like
.Fl bi .
.It Fl C Ar file
Ignored with a warning.
.It Fl B , Fl h , Fl L , Fl N , Fl O , Fl R , Fl V , Fl X , Fl p , Fl A
Take a value and are ignored.
.It Fl d , Fl e
Ignored; the value is glued or the next argument unless it starts with a
dash.
.It Fl v , Fl m , Fl n , Fl U , Fl G
Ignored.
.It Fl -config Ar path
Read another configuration file; ignored with a warning when the setgid
bit of the binary applies to a caller other than root.
.It Fl -version
Print the version.
.It Fl -help
Print a usage summary.
.El
.Pp
Called as
.Nm newaliases
the program does nothing; called as
.Nm mailq
it lists the queue.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev SLENDMAIL_CONFIG
Another configuration file, like
.Fl -config .
.It Ev EMAIL , Ev USER , Ev LOGNAME
Sender of a message without
.Fl f
and without a Resent-From or From header; ignored when the setgid bit
applies.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/slendmail.conf
The configuration.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
At least one target accepted the message, or a mode without a message
succeeded.
.It 64
Usage error: a sender flag without a value, a line break in an address
or in the full name,
.Fl bs ,
or a mode that does not exist yet.
.It 66
Standard input cannot be read.
.It 69
No target accepted the message.
.It 70
Internal error.
.It 77
A service mode requested by a caller without the right to it.
.It 78
The configuration cannot be read or is invalid.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr syslog 3 ,
.Xr cron 8
